#. what Grandmother says when all the animals are home; {rider} is the rider's name
#: data/levels/08_the_herders_request.tscn
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thank you, {rider}! Asking around helped!"
msgstr "Спасибо, {rider}! Расспросы помогли!"

#. what a person says to the rider, at most two short sentences; {rider} is her name
#: data/levels/08_the_herders_request.tscn
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our camels are gone, {rider}! Ask the shepherd at the well; he sees far."
msgstr "Наши верблюды пропали, {rider}! Спроси пастуха у колодца: он видит далеко."

#. what a person says to the rider, at most two short sentences; {rider} is her name
#: data/levels/08_the_herders_request.tscn
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good day, {rider}! The beekeeper by the birch grove saw your camels. And I saw sheep."
msgstr "Добрый день, {rider}! Пчеловод у берёзовой рощи видел твоих верблюдов. А я видел овец."

#. what a person says to the rider, at most two short sentences; {rider} is her name
#: data/levels/08_the_herders_request.tscn
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hello, {rider}! Yes, I saw your camels."
msgstr "Привет, {rider}! Да, я видела твоих верблюдов."

#. the name of a level, a few words
#: data/levels/09_autumn_migration.tscn
#, fuzzy
msgid "Autumn migration"
